  "body_text": "Our services\nEnvironmental DNA\n        Detect and monitor biodiversity through environmental DNA (eDNA) analysis.Applications :\n> Biodiversity surveys\n> Environmental impact assessments\n> Invasive species detection\n> Protected species monitoring\n\n Learn More\n            Population genomics\n        Assess the genetic diversity, connectivity, and adaptive potential of wild populations.\n Applications:> Conservation genetics> Population management> National Action Plans (NAPs)> Inbreeding, hybridization, and individual assignmentLearn More\n            Microbial Community Analysis\n        Study bacterial, fungal, and other microbial communities using high-throughput sequencing technologies.Applications:\n> Water quality assessment\n> Agricultural soil monitoring\n> Aquaculture\n> Research\nLearn More\n            Genomic seletion\n        Develop genomic selection tools to support breeding programs in the agricultural and aquaculture sectors.Applications:\n> Aquaculture\n> Agriculture\n> Genetic improvement\n    Learn More\n            Bioinformatics\n        Transform your sequencing data into actionable insights.Applications:\n> Metabarcoding & Metagenomics\n> RAD-seq & RNA-seq\n> Whole-Genome Sequencing (WGS)\n> Epigenetics\n> Genome-Wide Association Studies (GWAS)\n    Learn More\n            Sequencing & dPCR\n        Tailored sequencing and digital PCR (dPCR) solutions for your research and development projects.Applications:\n> Amplicon sequencing\n> Short- and long-read sequencing\n> Whole and partial genome sequencing\n> Target species and genetic variant detection\n    Learn More\n            Research & Development\n        Partner with LDgenX to accelerate your research and innovation projects.Applications:\n> Grant proposal support\n> Scientific consulting\n> Project support and guidance\n\nLet’s discuss your project\n        \n        Do you wish to implement biodiversity monitoring, study a population, or develop a specific molecular tool ?\n    \n                Contact our team",
  "metadata_path": "source/en/Services.json"
